CloudBurrow patch 76 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1622).

The bug: a jobs.insert naming a job ID the project already has ran the
job's query again, and only then, adding the job, failed with 400
jobInternalError "failed to add job: job <id> is already created". The
official Go client retries a jobs.insert with a jobReference after a
transient failure, when the first attempt may have made the job; its
retry then failed, and a DML statement ran a second time before the
error rolled it back. BigQuery answers such an insert 409 with reason
"duplicate" ("This error returns when trying to create a job, dataset,
or table that already exists",
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/error-messages) and runs nothing.

The patch looks the job up before jobs.insert runs anything and answers
409 duplicate, "Already Exists: Job project:LOCATION.id" (the location
the insert names, else US); AddJob's error is now a typed
DuplicatedJobError, which jobs.insert (two inserts of one ID at once) and
the upload handlers (a load's media, 500 internalError before) answer
the same way.

